* DATATYPE reports the runtime type name of the stored value, such as INTEGER or REAL.
* EQ signals success or failure. :S(YES)F(NO) uses that outcome to choose the branch.
    S = 'John'
    I = 6
    R = 1.1
    OUTPUT = DATATYPE(S)
    OUTPUT = DATATYPE(I)
    OUTPUT = DATATYPE(R)
    EQ(I,6) :S(YES)F(NO)
YES OUTPUT = 'TRUE' :(END)
NO OUTPUT = 'FALSE'
END
